Give the missing accent a name: --kavacha-accent-fallback

Kavacha ships no default accent on purpose (2026-07-13): the welcome flow
asks, and Midnight themes surfaces only. So until the user answers, BOTH
--zen-primary-color and --kavacha-accent are undefined -- a legitimate,
durable state that nothing named or documented. Every consumer had quietly
invented its own literal for it:

  studio.css:16       var(--zen-primary-color, var(--kavacha-accent, #8b7bd8))
  marketplace.css:17  var(--zen-primary-color, var(--kavacha-accent, #8b7bd8))
  plugins.css:17      var(--zen-primary-color, var(--kavacha-accent, #8b7bd8))

Three copies of one decision, stated in none of them. Anyone reading a line
would have to guess whether #8b7bd8 was a considered fallback, a placeholder,
or an accent someone forgot to wire up.

This adds --kavacha-accent-fallback to the 0016 baked floor, carrying the
policy in a comment where the value lives, and points the three consumers at
it. Rendering is unchanged -- the same colour resolves in the same cases --
but the empty accent is now a defined state instead of an accident, which is
what the defect asked for. It is explicitly NOT a default accent: nothing
assigns it to --zen-primary-color, it never enters Zen's colour-mix chain, and
any real accent still wins.

Worth recording: the token has to be declared TWICE, and that is not
redundancy. kavacha-midnight.inc.css is chrome CSS; about:studio,
about:marketplace and about:plugins are content documents and the chrome token
floor is simply not in their cascade. That is the actual reason those three
files hardcode fallbacks for every --kavacha-* token, not just the accent --
they can see none of them. Each declaration now says so and names the
canonical definition. Folding all of them into one shared content stylesheet
is the real fix; it needs a new jar entry and moz.build wiring, which cannot
be verified without a full build, so it is left as a follow-up rather than
guessed at here.

The companion half of this defect pair is documentation-only and lands outside
the patch chain, in the repo tree: customization/themes/kavacha-midnight/
colors.json and style.css now carry a $readBeforeEditing note explaining that
the package is a REFERENCE COPY -- the engine clears overrides for the default
theme and loads a package style.css only for user themes, so editing either
file changes nothing. That was D5, resolved as not-a-bug and kept open as a
maintenance trap. The note names both real sources (the 0016 baked floor and
BUILTIN_THEMES in KavachaThemeEngine.sys.mjs) and flags that only
surface/text/border are baked at all.

Not build-verified: CSS custom properties cannot be evaluated without a
running chrome. The change is declaration-only -- no selector, no cascade
order, no existing declaration altered except the three accent expressions.
diff --git a/src/zen/kavacha-theme/kavacha-midnight.inc.css b/src/zen/kavacha-theme/kavacha-midnight.inc.css
--- a/src/zen/kavacha-theme/kavacha-midnight.inc.css
+++ b/src/zen/kavacha-theme/kavacha-midnight.inc.css
@@ -29,6 +29,26 @@
   --kavacha-text-primary: #edeaf7;
   --kavacha-text-secondary: #a79fc4;
 
+  /* The colour to use when no accent has been chosen yet.
+
+     Kavacha ships no default accent by decision (2026-07-13, see header): the
+     welcome flow asks, and until it is answered BOTH --zen-primary-color and
+     --kavacha-accent are undefined. That gap is legitimate and durable -- a
+     user may simply never pick one -- but it had no name, so every consumer
+     invented its own literal for it and none of them said what it was. An
+     absent accent is a defined state now, not an accident.
+
+     This is NOT a default accent. Nothing assigns it to --zen-primary-color,
+     it never reaches Zen's colour-mix chain, and any real accent -- from the
+     welcome flow or from a theme package -- wins over it. Consume it last:
+
+       var(--zen-primary-color, var(--kavacha-accent, var(--kavacha-accent-fallback)))
+
+     Content documents (about:studio, about:marketplace, about:plugins) are
+     not in this stylesheet's cascade and each redeclare the token; keep those
+     in step with this value. */
+  --kavacha-accent-fallback: #8b7bd8;
+
   /* The base every --zen-colors-* mix derives from. */
   --zen-branding-dark: var(--kavacha-surface);
 
diff --git a/src/zen/kavacha-studio/studio.css b/src/zen/kavacha-studio/studio.css
